  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> Bulky base is present, it will abstract proton, hence will undergo E2 reaction<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/czyggjzyqnmxsfazpyoywcmtuugsdjuqipsaforyfrglfeygfn.jpeg\"/><br ><math><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> Hydrogen ion will protonate the oxygen of methoxy group and make it a good leaving group, hence methanol and t-butyl bromide is formed.<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/tczufshwcrtkkcashrwupxcxdwguxyiucufrdvuiqoaarouzxi.jpeg\"/><br ><math><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> Methoxy group will abstract proton. E2 elimination occur<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/wxvhlozfjwpqkxrrncznnqwkyzddfnadqpwskavpbjvgejdnju.jpeg\"/><br ><math><mo>(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>)</mo></math> It will undergo <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math> mechanism.<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/kwvwecrknvxhgstaiqnbdjiztfcykjlwtgocjqhfqyxogsoaww.jpeg\"/>",
